  <section id="tax-revenue">
    <h2>Tax Revenue Trajectory, 2020 – 2025</h2>

    <p>Maine raises cannabis tax revenue from two streams: (1) <strong>AUCP fees and excise</strong> collected by the Office of Cannabis Policy, deposited via the State Controller to the General Fund with retention for OCP regulatory operations; and (2) the <strong>5.5% general state sales tax</strong> on medical cannabis (8% on edible cannabis products as prepared food), collected by Maine Revenue Services and deposited in the General Fund. Both streams are reported annually; the figures below combine both.</p>

